When Republicans talk about “essential services,” they don’t mean for you. | | | Friend — When Republicans talk about “essential services,” they don’t mean for you. They mean******ballroom renovations, corporate tax breaks, and kickbacks for their donors** , even while shutting down the government and leaving working families wondering when their next paycheck will come. Elizabeth Guzman knows what essential really means. ✅ **Teachers.** Because every child deserves a fair shot. ✅ **Nurses.** Because our communities can’t run without care. ✅ **Public workers.****** Because government isn’t the problem. The problem is the people who sabotage it. As a social worker, immigrant, and mom, Elizabeth’s spent her life fighting for those essential workers, the ones who keep Virginia running even when politicians play games. But her opponent, Ian Lovejoy, voted with the far right to slash funding for special education schools, health care, and public safety — **_then called his own salary essential._** Let’s remind them who this government really serves. **[Can you chip in today to help Elizabeth keep fighting for the people who make Virginia work every day?](https://click.actionnetwork.org/ss/c/u001.iIBo0N5fSFzEFL40Tn-vtbMETCUYClkOrOh9-SNJfqvhsqD6hnNNbCP7JMDskKO3XlC2dXs5AeG50ELm382_QLviQ9RVLlw2kiw7ipnP7rAJbPwCp266bmXfp0Zxii0Me8CIbFfv1G-OJOZbCY_k6wVJGYAFEOh6N4vryOLHDOLIJkKWM7rV6Qlj-ngs5Pgl8gs83cX46qNwEriAx1QsfDEBMkrUkELwusTieT-p-JgwfqYgwch93u490zahiznL3LdC4kUxU-4XpRllaT-bvlNRewvdY69KGuuPIkEEFyJJutUdQ4wcY4_-9I9vEAmDE62Mx8vKW-R06mQwRqc-piRMAhhqXUj0BQLJ5xOiCoiTuwz9u_IMFvdbQtRSA6EKRjkiLVdJqpdsm-9CeUpDV_OYs6-q2p1VeITDU6TtsA8/4ks/V_3PrHs4R6eaNiD8NETVhA/h0/h001.56jq4v-huu4itVoFHiXOCNA2ljpwdlW5kQXtUzXfl3k)** _If you've saved your payment information with ActBlue Express, your donation will go through immediately._ [Donate $10
